  "description": "<p>In the HTML UI browsing to an RDFSource object's versions (<a href=\"http://localhost:8080/rest/apple_box/carton_of_apples/fcr:versions\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/rest/apple_box/carton_of_apples/fcr:versions</a>) results in being redirected to non-existant fcr:metadata (<a href=\"http://localhost:8080/rest/apple_box/carton_of_apples/fcr:versions/fcr:metadata\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/rest/apple_box/carton_of_apples/fcr:versions/fcr:metadata</a>) because the original URI does not return a Link Header (which is how we determine a RDFSource).<br/>\n<a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/blob/master/fcrepo-http-api/src/main/resources/views/common.js#L96\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/blob/master/fcrepo-http-api/src/main/resources/views/common.js#L96</a></p>\n\n<p>Possibly twitchy solution is to not redirect if the URI ends in \"/fcr:*\"</p>",
